    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s narrow streets once housed low‑rise homes that blended Jugendstil and early Bauhaus design, some even featuring private bathrooms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neve_Tzedek"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, Neve Tzedek attracted writers like Shmuel Yosef Agnon and artist Nachum Gutman, turning it into Tel Aviv’s cultural hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neve_Tzedek"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 130‑year‑old building in Neve Tzedek now hosts the Nahum Gutman Museum, honoring the painter’s legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visit-tel-aviv.com/en/Neve-Tzedek"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Suzanne Dellal Centre for Dance and Theatre, established in the quarter, brought contemporary performing arts to the historic streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://travelsetu.com/guide/neve-tzedek-quarter-tourism/neve-tzedek-quarter-tourism-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "After decades of neglect, a 1970s public campaign saved Neve Tzedek from demolition, sparking its 1990s revival as a bohemian enclave.",
